[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. The reports merged
into it say three. They were merged because their subject lines looked alike
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)); nobody had to read the bodies, so nobody
did. One fix will not close them all.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three problems, three tickets. Fixing the parser closes only the first.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## Where they stand

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October:

| problem | ticket | state |
|---|---|---|
| `parser` | [#1](https://github.com/dawidkotowicz/MegaDev/issues/1) | closed, fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | [#2](https://github.com/dawidkotowicz/MegaDev/issues/2) | closed, won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired |
| `move` | [#3](https://github.com/dawidkotowicz/MegaDev/issues/3) | **open**: neither change touches it |

Closing #4471 did not close `move`. A one-day shift still reaches invites and reminders.

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first. A booking for 7 April (07/04) goes out as 4 July. This is what #4471 describes, and
the fix queued for it.

**`hint` — booking-v3 tells people to type the month first.** The booking-v3 form prints
`MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then reads what people type the tenant's way, day first.
It only happens on the form channel of tenants who run booking-v3. These reports look the same
as `parser` from the outside: day and month swapped. Fixing the parser does not touch the form,
so they keep coming after #4471 closes.

**`move` — the date moves by exactly one day.** No day and month swap at all: "Tuesday 12 May"
shown as "Monday 11 May", a meeting held on Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto, every June
booking one day off. The desk already read these as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) but left
them filed under `parser`, as a footnote. A month-first parser cannot move a date by one day;
this looks like a time zone or daylight-saving shift. It needs its own ticket and its own owner.

## Why intake tags do not help

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser the moment it arrives. The problem depends on
the tenant: where they are, and which booking form they run (`locales.ts`). A tenant's client on
an `en-US` browser is still a day-first tenant. The table counts how many reports carry the wrong
tag.

## What the desk's own table shows

The table on #4471, built by `CauseTable`, already splits `parser` from `hint`, but marks `hint`
as "no ticket of its own" and hides `move` in a footnote:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes

- Each problem has its own ticket, with its own count. Close each one on its own fix.
- When #4471 closes, watch for new date reports from booking-v3 forms and one-day moves: they
  are not fixed by the parser.
- Merging on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put three
  problems into one ticket. Before you merge a report into a big ticket, check its cause with
  [the dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe), and read the body when it does not say day and month
  swapped. Changing the rule needs a new decision record; 0001 stays as it is.

